course: dictionary
lesson: 4613
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word hide can mean put out of sight, keep a feeling secret, or a hut for watching birds. «When they bow, their curly wigs get tangled, and Alice has to run off to hide her laughter.» Here, hide means keep it secret, because she is trying not to be seen laughing.
explain: Read the words around the word. «The bird watchers waited quietly in a hide by the lake.» Waiting quietly by a lake tells you a hide is a small hut, not a animal's skin. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence best? Then try it in place of the word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Hide can also be a noun, a thing rather than an action. «Leather is made from an animal's hide.» Here, hide means skin. Watch for small clues like a, an, or the, which often show the word is a thing.
fact: Hide can mean to put something where it cannot be seen or found.
fact: Hide can mean to keep a feeling or a secret, so nobody knows about it.
fact: A hide is also a small hut where people watch birds or animals without being seen.
fact: «Hiding it is worse than paying for it» shows that hiding a problem can make it bigger.
fact: Safety rule: never hide in a fridge, a car boot, or any place you cannot get out of.
exercise: «When they bow, their curly wigs get tangled, and Alice has to run off to hide her laughter.» What does hide mean here? | *Keep her laughter secret | Shout her laughter loudly | Eat her laughter quickly | Put her laughter in a box
exercise: «The Year 3s hid behind the climbing frame whenever Jake walked past.» What does hid mean? | Painted the climbing frame | *Went where others could not see them | Built a new climbing frame | Ran races around the climbing frame
exercise: «The bird watchers waited quietly in a hide by the lake.» What is a hide in this sentence? | Tree roots growing in the mud | A loud whistle used at football | *A small hut where people watch birds without being seen | An animal's skin used for leather
test: «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying, but it can hide things.» What does hide most likely mean? | Sing loudly | *Keep out of sight or secret | Show clearly | Read aloud
test: «If you lose or damage a library book, you tell the librarian honestly; hiding it is worse than paying for it.» What does hiding mean here? | *Keeping the problem secret | Sending it to a friend | Putting it back on the shelf | Reading it quickly
exam: Which place is never safe to hide in? | Behind the sofa in your own home | *Inside an old fridge | Under your bed at home | Behind a big tree in the park
